{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  QUICK SETTINGS — what the app bar's avatar opens
  REFERENCE §7.2, AppBar.dc.html
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  A short sheet: who you are, text size, the two switches people reach for most,
  the languages, and a way through to all of them. It exists so the phone bar can
  hold ONE button instead of three — §18.5 rejects a bar carrying back, title,
  search, Aa, language and avatar, and this is where the Aa and the globe went.

  ── IT IS A SUBSET, NOT A SECOND SET ─────────────────────────────────────────

  Two of the seven switches are here and all seven are one tap away. Every control
  writes the same `ag-a11y` store through `AGA11y.set()`, and the store fires
  `ag:a11y` on every write, so the copy inside the Menu and the copy on the full
  screen re-read rather than keeping their own idea of what is on. This codebase's
  standing fault is two surfaces disagreeing about one setting; three doors onto
  one store is the answer to it, and three stores would be the fault.

  ── THE LANGUAGE CHIPS SCROLL, AND THAT IS A DECISION ────────────────────────

  Eight chips do not fit across 390px. They scroll horizontally here because the
  sheet is a shortcut; the Menu's sub-view and the full screen both present the
  same eight as a vertical list, where nothing is off-screen. A horizontal scroller
  is acceptable for a shortcut and is not acceptable as the only way to reach an
  option — which is why it is never the only way.
#}
{% set _ini = member_name ? (member_name|split(' ')|map(w => w|first)|join|upper|slice(0,2)) : 'AG' %}
{# See the note in menu-sheet.twig: `hidden` is display:none and defeats `data-open`. #}
<div class="ag-scrim" data-ag-quick-scrim></div>

<div class="ag-sheet ag-qs" data-ag-quick-sheet role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-label="Account, language and display" inert>

  <span class="ag-sheet__grabber" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="ag-qs__body">

    {% if is_member %}
      <a class="ag-qs__me" href="/account">
        <span class="ag-menu__av">{{ _ini }}</span>
        <span class="ag-menu__who">
          <b>{{ member_name|default('Your account') }}</b>
          <span>View your profile</span>
        </span>
        <span class="ag-list__chev" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
               stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
        </span>
      </a>
    {% else %}
      <a class="ag-btn ag-btn--ink ag-btn--block" href="/account/login">Sign in or join</a>
    {% endif %}

    {# The same three-step control as everywhere else, at the 48px height §7.2
       asks for rather than DisplayReading's 44. The letters are drawn at the
       sizes they set; the accessible name carries the words. #}
    <div class="ag-qs__block">
      <span class="ag-qs__h" id="ag-qs-size">Text size</span>
      <div class="ag-seg ag-seg--48" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="ag-qs-size">
        {# The size is a class, never a `style` attribute — see display-reading.twig. #}
        {% for s in [
          {i:0, name:'Standard text'},
          {i:1, name:'Large text'},
          {i:2, name:'Largest text'}
        ] %}
          <button type="button" class="ag-seg__opt ag-dr__size ag-dr__size--{{ s.i }}" role="radio"
                  aria-checked="false" aria-label="{{ s.name }}"
                  data-ag-size="{{ s.i }}">A</button>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ag-dr ag-qs__switches">
      {% for t in [
        {k:'hc',     label:'High contrast', help:'Darker text and borders'},
        {k:'motion', label:'Reduce motion', help:'No animation or auto-play'}
      ] %}
        <button type="button" class="ag-dr__row" role="switch" aria-checked="false"
                data-ag-toggle="{{ t.k }}">
          <span class="ag-dr__text">
            <span class="ag-dr__label">{{ t.label }}</span>
            <span class="ag-dr__help">{{ t.help }}</span>
          </span>
          <span class="ag-switch" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="ag-qs__block">
      <span class="ag-qs__h" id="ag-qs-lang">Language</span>
      {# Each chip carries `lang` so a screen reader pronounces the word in its own
         language instead of reading "Yorùbá" as English. Links, not radios: following
         one navigates, and the middleware is what stores the choice — so these work
         with scripting off, which for a language control matters most. #}
      <nav class="ag-qs__langs" aria-labelledby="ag-qs-lang">
        {% for l in languages() %}
          <a class="ag-chip ag-qs__lang" href="{{ lang_url(l.code) }}" lang="{{ l.code }}"
             {{ l.code == lang() ? 'aria-current="true"' : '' }}>{{ l.name }}</a>
        {% endfor %}
      </nav>
    </div>

    <button type="button" class="ag-list__row ag-qs__all" data-ag-quick-all>
      <span class="ag-list__label">All display &amp; reading settings</span>
      <span class="ag-list__chev" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
             stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"></path></svg>
      </span>
    </button>

    {# Done rather than a close cross: this sheet has no destructive state and
       nothing to cancel, so the one button says what pressing it means. #}
    <button type="button" class="ag-btn ag-btn--ink ag-btn--block ag-qs__done"
            data-ag-quick-close>Done</button>
  </div>
</div>
